#: ../../source/docs/editing-prs.rst:5
#: b760ec68880945ef9724524a8616bfb2
msgid "How to Edit Someone Else's PR Directly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-prs.rst:7
#: e26de5ac35df4d71914d337651fb3166
msgid "Occasionally, it is desirable to make some small changes to someone else's submitted PR in order to facilitate its readiness for merging. This describes one procedure for doing this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-prs.rst:10
#: a542e791e247465cb535fc75c667d62f
msgid "Assumptions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-prs.rst:12
#: 65f127e5cef14427b6943b6f690819fe
msgid "It is assumed that you have worked on the GitHub repository for ArduPilot before and have cloned a fork of the repository locally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-prs.rst:15
#: 91b125af61bf4966ba5faaf5f13f030f
msgid "Procedure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-prs.rst:17
#: 0bba9ea77ef5453a8487f2d89026fd11
msgid "First, determine if you have been given permission to modify the PR. If so, then at the bottom of the PR on GitHub.com you will see :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-prs.rst:19
#: 78d875637704433ab0404432d2d8af27
msgid "\"Add more commits by pushing to the ``xyz`` branch on ``username/ardupilot``\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-prs.rst:21
#: 1de0d338ec2d48dca707fe4ba3c0a9c7
msgid "First set up a remote to username's repository, in this case we will call it ``tempremote`` :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-prs.rst:27
#: 0800147783184eb8a719f784d8ad2aaa
msgid "this sets up ``tempremote`` to point to the originators repository on GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-prs.rst:29
#: 5d528944164244759e7a7bdf9f9fb9c8
msgid "To pull the PR branch ``xyz`` down to your local computer's repository in order to modify it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-prs.rst:35
#: db20629bbe594dd18b47108f416a2251
msgid "which will copy the PR's branch into a local buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-prs.rst:37
#: dd1fe65d0ed44b8e8b05ca21e45e07e1
msgid "Then create a local branch ``username-xyz`` and which is a copy of the PR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-prs.rst:44
#: a67852014d074535beb8f59d2a503c49
msgid "Next make your mods and commit them with a commit message explaining your changes. This message will actually be removed in the next step, but it's good to make it something meaningful if you need to reset or revert in the future."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-prs.rst:46
#: fd501edd3c6248d89f15c5e8d0a61539
msgid "You should also \"squash\" (see :ref:`git-interactive-rebase` ) your commit into the originator's before pushing to his repository yourself. At this point you can use the originator's commit message or change it if it needs. Also, you should be sure that the entire commit conforms to the ArduPilot style guidelines (see :ref:`style-guide` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-prs.rst:48
#: e40f80f1f6b04be0bff19706d4a753c2
msgid "Finally, you can force push over the originators PR to include your modifications:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/editing-prs.rst:54
#: 0f8d5970d8c74d6fa5ce02cadb13d04a
msgid "The changes will be reflected in the PR on GitHub. You may now delete your ``username-xyz`` branch locally."
msgstr ""
